730105). Altogether, the association of this allele to IGHV3-43D is reasonable. IARC affirms the sequence at level 1 up to and including base 321 in agreement with past practice. It is acknowledged that the allele most likely carries one additional base, typically A at base position 322. A trailing “.” indicates IARC’s opinion that the sequence is likely to contain one additional 3’-nucleotides for which there is insufficient evidence to make an affirmation. The allele is given the name IGHV3-43D*i02.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'',0,NULL,NULL,'Mats Ohlin',NULL,'Homo sapiens','','none',1,297,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'1','likely_truncated','F',NULL,NULL,76,99,151,174,289,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL),(2559,'IGHV1-69*i04','A02559','Dept. of Immunotechnology, Lund University, Medicon Village building 406, S-22381 Lund, Sweden',2,'2023-07-10 00:00:00','(D) removed from name as this designation is not used in the AIRR-C human germline sets','IGHV1-69*06 G240A,IGHV1-69(D)*i04','IGH','V','Rearranged Only','1','superceded','1','1-69(D)','i04','CAGGTGCAGCTGGTGCAGTCTGGGGCTGAGGTGAAGAAGCCTGGGTCCTCGGTGAAGGTCTCCTGCAAGGCTTCTGGAGGCACCTTCAGCAGCTATGCTATCAGCTGGGTGCGACAGGCCCCTGGACAAGGGCTTGAGTGGATGGGAGGGATCATCCCTATCTTTGGTACAGCAAACTACGCACAGAAGTTCCAGGGCAGAGTCACGATTACCGCAGACAAATCCACGAGCACAGCCTACATGGAGCTGAGCAGCCTGAGATCTGAGGACACGGCCGTGTATTACTGTGCGAGAG.','CAGGTGCAGCTGGTGCAGTCTGGGGCT...GAGGTGAAGAAGCCTGGGTCCTCGGTGAAGGTCTCCTGCAAGGCTTCTGGAGGCACCTTC............AGCAGCTATGCTATCAGCTGGGTGCGACAGGCCCCTGGACAAGGGCTTGAGTGGATGGGAGGGATCATCCCTATC......TTTGGTACAGCAAACTACGCACAGAAGTTCCAG...GGCAGAGTCACGATTACCGCAGACAAATCCACGAGCACAGCCTACATGGAGCTGAGCAGCCTGAGATCTGAGGACACGGCCGTGTATTACTGTGCGAGAG.',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'','This inferred allele was assessed at IARC meeting 100 on June 8th, 2022. IGHV1-69*06_G240A was inferred in subject S45 (VDJ-base: P1_I48_S1). The genotype also carried IGHV1-69*01 and IGHV1-69*06. Given t